#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:1
msgid "Release 2.4 (2021-11-01)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:3
msgid ""
"This is the first release in more than two years and is the result of more "
"than 2800 commits from 195 contributors since release 2.3."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:6
msgid "Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:8
msgid ""
"Nix's **error messages** have been improved a lot. For instance, evaluation "
"errors now point out the location of the error:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:23
msgid ""
"The **`nix` command** has seen a lot of work and is now almost at feature "
"parity with the old command-line interface (the `nix-*` commands). It aims "
"to be [more modern, consistent and pleasant to use](../development/cli-"
"guideline.md) than the old CLI. It is still marked as experimental but its "
"interface should not change much anymore in future releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:30
msgid ""
"**Flakes** are a new format to package Nix-based projects in a more "
"discoverable, composable, consistent and reproducible way. A flake is just a "
"repository or tarball containing a file named `flake.nix` that specifies "
"dependencies on other flakes and returns any Nix assets such as packages, "
"Nixpkgs overlays, NixOS modules or CI tests. The new `nix` CLI is primarily "
"based around flakes; for example, a command like `nix run nixpkgs#hello` "
"runs the `hello` application from the `nixpkgs` flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:39
msgid ""
"Flakes are currently marked as experimental. For an introduction, see [this "
"blog post](https://www.tweag.io/blog/2020-05-25-flakes/). For detailed "
"information about flake syntax and semantics, see the [`nix flake` manual "
"page](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:45
msgid ""
"Nix's store can now be **content-addressed**, meaning that the hash "
"component of a store path is the hash of the path's contents. Previously Nix "
"could only build **input-addressed** store paths, where the hash is computed "
"from the derivation dependency graph. Content-addressing allows "
"deduplication, early cutoff in build systems, and unprivileged closure "
"copying. This is still [an experimental feature](https://discourse.nixos.org/"
"t/content-addressed-nix-call-for-testers/12881)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:54
msgid ""
"The Nix manual has been converted into Markdown, making it easier to "
"contribute. In addition, every `nix` subcommand now has a manual page, "
"documenting every option."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:58
msgid ""
"A new setting that allows **experimental features** to be enabled "
"selectively. This allows us to merge unstable features into Nix more quickly "
"and do more frequent releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:62
msgid "Other features"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:64
msgid "There are many new `nix` subcommands:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:66
msgid ""
"`nix develop` is intended to replace `nix-shell`. It has a number of new "
"features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:69
msgid ""
"It automatically sets the output environment variables (such as `$out`) to "
"writable locations (such as `./outputs/out`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:72
msgid ""
"It can store the environment in a profile. This is useful for offline work."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:75
msgid ""
"It can run specific phases directly. For instance, `nix develop --build` "
"runs `buildPhase`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:78
msgid ""
"It allows dependencies in the Nix store to be \"redirected\" to arbitrary "
"directories using the `--redirect` flag. This is useful if you want to hack "
"on a package _and_ some of its dependencies at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:83
msgid ""
"`nix print-dev-env` prints the environment variables and bash functions "
"defined by a derivation. This is useful for users of other shells than bash "
"(especially with `--json`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:87
msgid ""
"`nix shell` was previously named `nix run` and is intended to replace `nix-"
"shell -p`, but without the `stdenv` overhead. It simply starts a shell where "
"some packages have been added to `$PATH`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:92
msgid ""
"`nix run` (not to be confused with the old subcommand that has been renamed "
"to `nix shell`) runs an \"app\", a flake output that specifies a command to "
"run, or an eponymous program from a package. For example, `nix run "
"nixpkgs#hello` runs the `hello` program from the `hello` package in "
"`nixpkgs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:98
msgid ""
"`nix flake` is the container for flake-related operations, such as creating "
"a new flake, querying the contents of a flake or updating flake lock files."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:102
msgid ""
"`nix registry` allows you to query and update the flake registry, which maps "
"identifiers such as `nixpkgs` to concrete flake URLs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:105
msgid ""
"`nix profile` is intended to replace `nix-env`. Its main advantage is that "
"it keeps track of the provenance of installed packages (e.g. exactly which "
"flake version a package came from). It also has some helpful subcommands:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:110
msgid ""
"`nix profile history` shows what packages were added, upgraded or removed "
"between each version of a profile."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:113
msgid ""
"`nix profile diff-closures` shows the changes between the closures of each "
"version of a profile. This allows you to discover the addition or removal of "
"dependencies or size changes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:118
msgid ""
"**Warning**: after a profile has been updated using `nix profile`, it is no "
"longer usable with `nix-env`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:121
msgid ""
"`nix store diff-closures` shows the differences between the closures of two "
"store paths in terms of the versions and sizes of dependencies in the "
"closures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:125
msgid ""
"`nix store make-content-addressable` rewrites an arbitrary closure to make "
"it content-addressed. Such paths can be copied into other stores without "
"requiring signatures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:129
msgid ""
"`nix bundle` uses the [`nix-bundle` program](https://github.com/matthewbauer/"
"nix-bundle) to convert a closure into a self-extracting executable."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:133
msgid ""
"Various other replacements for the old CLI, e.g. `nix store gc`, `nix store "
"delete`, `nix store repair`, `nix nar dump-path`, `nix store prefetch-file`, "
"`nix store prefetch-tarball`, `nix key` and `nix daemon`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:138
msgid ""
"Nix now has an **evaluation cache** for flake outputs. For example, a second "
"invocation of the command `nix run nixpkgs#firefox` will not need to "
"evaluate the `firefox` attribute because it's already in the evaluation "
"cache. This is made possible by the hermetic evaluation model of flakes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:144
msgid "Intermediate results are not cached."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:146
msgid ""
"The new `--offline` flag disables substituters and causes all locally cached "
"tarballs and repositories to be considered up-to-date."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:150
msgid ""
"The new `--refresh` flag causes all locally cached tarballs and repositories "
"to be considered out-of-date."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:153
msgid ""
"Many `nix` subcommands now have a `--json` option to produce machine-"
"readable output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:156
msgid ""
"`nix repl` has a new `:doc` command to show documentation about builtin "
"functions (e.g. `:doc builtins.map`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:159
msgid ""
"Binary cache stores now have an option `index-debug-info` to create an index "
"of DWARF debuginfo files for use by [`dwarffs`](https://github.com/edolstra/"
"dwarffs)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:163
msgid ""
"To support flakes, Nix now has an extensible mechanism for fetching source "
"trees. Currently it has the following backends:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:166
msgid "Git repositories"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:168
msgid "Mercurial repositories"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:170
msgid ""
"GitHub and GitLab repositories (an optimisation for faster fetching than Git)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:173
msgid "Tarballs"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:175
msgid "Arbitrary directories"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:177
msgid ""
"The fetcher infrastructure is exposed via flake input specifications and via "
"the `fetchTree` built-in."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:180
msgid ""
"**Languages changes**: the only new language feature is that you can now "
"have antiquotations in paths, e.g. `./${foo}` instead of `./. + foo`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:184
msgid "**New built-in functions**:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:186
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchTree` allows fetching a source tree using any backends "
"supported by the fetcher infrastructure. It subsumes the functionality of "
"existing built-ins like `fetchGit`, `fetchMercurial` and `fetchTarball`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:191
msgid ""
"`builtins.getFlake` fetches a flake and returns its output attributes. This "
"function should not be used inside flakes! Use flake inputs instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:195
msgid ""
"`builtins.floor` and `builtins.ceil` round a floating-point number down and "
"up, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:198
msgid ""
"Experimental support for recursive Nix. This means that Nix derivations can "
"now call Nix to build other derivations. This is not in a stable state yet "
"and not well [documented](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"c4d7c76b641d82b2696fef73ce0ac160043c18da)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:203
msgid ""
"The new experimental feature `no-url-literals` disables URL literals. This "
"helps to implement [RFC 45](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/pull/45)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:207
msgid ""
"Nix now uses `libarchive` to decompress and unpack tarballs and zip files, "
"so `tar` is no longer required."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:210
msgid ""
"The priority of substituters can now be overridden using the `priority` "
"substituter setting (e.g. `--substituters 'http://cache.nixos.org?"
"priority=100 daemon?priority=10'`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:214
msgid ""
"`nix edit` now supports non-derivation attributes, e.g. `nix edit ."
"#nixosConfigurations.bla`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:217
msgid ""
"The `nix` command now provides command line completion for `bash`, `zsh` and "
"`fish`. Since the support for getting completions is built into `nix`, it's "
"easy to add support for other shells."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:221
msgid ""
"The new `--log-format` flag selects what Nix's output looks like. It "
"defaults to a terse progress indicator. There is a new `internal-json` "
"output format for use by other programs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:225
msgid ""
"`nix eval` has a new `--apply` flag that applies a function to the "
"evaluation result."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:228
msgid ""
"`nix eval` has a new `--write-to` flag that allows it to write a nested "
"attribute set of string leaves to a corresponding directory tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:232
msgid ""
"Memory improvements: many operations that add paths to the store or copy "
"paths between stores now run in constant memory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:235
msgid ""
"Many `nix` commands now support the flag `--derivation` to operate on a `."
"drv` file itself instead of its outputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:238
msgid ""
"There is a new store called `dummy://` that does not support building or "
"adding paths. This is useful if you want to use the Nix evaluator but don't "
"have a Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:242
msgid ""
"The `ssh-ng://` store now allows substituting paths on the remote, as `ssh://"
"` already did."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:245
msgid ""
"When auto-calling a function with an ellipsis, all arguments are now passed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:248
msgid "New `nix-shell` features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:250
msgid ""
"It preserves the `PS1` environment variable if `NIX_SHELL_PRESERVE_PROMPT` "
"is set."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:253
msgid "With `-p`, it passes any `--arg`s as Nixpkgs arguments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:255
msgid "Support for structured attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:257
msgid "`nix-prefetch-url` has a new `--executable` flag."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:259
msgid ""
"On `x86_64` systems, [`x86_64` microarchitecture levels](https://lwn.net/"
"Articles/844831/) are mapped to additional system types (e.g. `x86_64-v1-"
"linux`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:263
msgid ""
"The new `--eval-store` flag allows you to use a different store for "
"evaluation than for building or storing the build result. This is primarily "
"useful when you want to query whether something exists in a read-only store, "
"such as a binary cache:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:268
msgid ""
"```\n"
"# nix path-info --json --store https://cache.nixos.org \\\n"
"  --eval-store auto nixpkgs#hello\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:273
msgid "(Here `auto` indicates the local store.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:275
msgid ""
"The Nix daemon has a new low-latency mechanism for copying closures. This is "
"useful when building on remote stores such as `ssh-ng://`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:279
msgid "Plugins can now register `nix` subcommands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:281
msgid ""
"The `--indirect` flag to `nix-store --add-root` has become a no-op. `--add-"
"root` will always generate indirect GC roots from now on."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:284
msgid "Incompatible changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:286
msgid ""
"The `nix` command is now marked as an experimental feature. This means that "
"you need to add"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:293
msgid ""
"to your `nix.conf` if you want to use it, or pass `--extra-experimental-"
"features nix-command` on the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:296
msgid ""
"The `nix` command no longer has a syntax for referring to packages in a "
"channel. This means that the following no longer works:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:303
msgid ""
"Instead, you can either use the `#` syntax to select a package from a flake, "
"e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:310
msgid ""
"Or, if you want to use the `nixpkgs` channel in the `NIX_PATH` environment "
"variable:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:317
msgid ""
"The old `nix run` has been renamed to `nix shell`, while there is a new `nix "
"run` that runs a default command. So instead of"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:324
msgid "you should use"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:330
msgid "or just"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:336
msgid "if the command you want to run has the same name as the package."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:338
msgid ""
"It is now an error to modify the `plugin-files` setting via a command-line "
"flag that appears after the first non-flag argument to any command, "
"including a subcommand to `nix`. For example, `nix-instantiate default.nix --"
"plugin-files \"\"` must now become `nix-instantiate --plugin-files \"\" "
"default.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.4.md:344
msgid ""
"We no longer release source tarballs. If you want to build from source, "
"please build from the tags in the Git repository."
msgstr ""

